edit(5,'guardrails',rows[4]['guardrails']+' Every concrete state and command field is listed as mapped or explicitly reviewed quotient/stutter/ghost-only; an unlisted field fails coverage. Quotients preserve authentication/binding identity, clock/deadline and outcome meaning; reviewed opaque-nonce renaming is allowed without erasing those relations.','Total field coverage with explicit limited equivalence.')
ss=rows[4]['scenarios'];ss.append({'name':'unlisted-field-mutation','given':'a runtime mutant drops an Unknown reservation or changes an undeclared field','when':'abstraction coverage and coupled replay run','then':'verification fails at that field rather than silently observing only the visible model'})
edit(5,'scenarios',ss,'Add non-vacuous field-coverage witness.')
ss=rows[5]['scenarios'];ss[1]['given']='a malformed, untrusted or unauthorized payload that fails boundary admission';ss[1]['then']='no admitted event, native mutation or transaction settlement is produced; only a bounded allowlisted rejection diagnostic is retained, with no fabricated Refused outcome';ss.append({'name':'authenticated-historical-reconciliation','given':'an exact authenticated historical receipt for a retained obligation and its declared reconciliation route','when':'it arrives after frontend replacement','then':'only the historical obligation may settle; the receipt grants no authority to the replacement binding and renews no deadline'})
edit(6,'scenarios',ss,'Separate malformed rejection from valid historical proof.')
edit(6,'guardrails',rows[5]['guardrails']+' Terminal Refused requires exact authenticated native evidence or a validated definitive unsent certificate. Historical proof admission follows its explicit recovery contract.','No fabricated refusal.')
edit(7,'ears',"WHEN a native effect depends on a prerequisite, the controller SHALL admit its request only after matching authenticated evidence satisfies that operation's protocol-specific prerequisite, while native authority revalidates the dependency at commit.",'Native remains serialization authority; commitment cannot stand for presentation or physical cleanup.')
edit(7,'baselineIds',sorted(set(rows[6]['baselineIds']+['ELM-ARC-008','ELM-ARC-012'])),'Exact baseline native dependency mapping.')
edit(7,'guardrails',rows[6]['guardrails']+' Native revalidates prerequisite incarnation, generation and dependency revision. Preview drain/release/presentation require their own evidence; a window Committed receipt cannot substitute.','No frontend-only dependency authority.')
edit(8,'ears','WHEN a protocol event is received, each participant SHALL admit it only under the declared actor-specific transitions, version and outcome reachability with exact correlation; otherwise it SHALL reject it without authority, ownership or settlement effect and retain a bounded rejection diagnostic.','Illegal receive is fail-closed; diagnosis is not terminal refusal.')
edit(8,'baselineIds',sorted(set(rows[7]['baselineIds']+['ELM-ARC-004','ELM-ARC-007'])),'Protocol boundary/outcome mappings.')
edit(10,'tradeoffs','Metadata and clock/queue instrumentation; frontend timers may provide feedback or fail-closed withdrawal of unsent local intent, but cannot authorize, extend, settle or time native work or substitute for native original deadlines. Vector clocks are unnecessary.','Safe local fail-closed timers remain permitted.')
edit(11,'guardrails',rows[10]['guardrails'].replace('actionable localized text','actionable, reviewed text from a catalog that supports localization')+' Supporting localization does not add a translation release gate.','No silent localization scope expansion.')
ss=rows[11]['scenarios'];ss[1]['then']='a distinct policy-eligible update is exposed without restarting the effect or changing its deadline; unauthenticated, unrelated or unauthorized receipts cause no update, while exact authenticated historical evidence may reconcile retained Unknown through the declared recovery route'
edit(12,'scenarios',ss,'Old epoch is not necessarily foreign or unauthorized.')
edit(13,'baselineIds',sorted(set(rows[12]['baselineIds']+['ELM-QA-021','ELM-QA-023','ELM-REV-020','ELM-REV-021'])),'Use actual frozen budget IDs; no invented ELM-PER IDs.')
edit(13,'guardrails','Secrets, credentials, draft contents and captured pixels are always excluded from ordinary diagnostics under ELM-DEL-017. Raw port bodies, titles, arguments and paths are also excluded by this ordinary allowlist. A different scoped mode requires a separate reviewed contract and is outside this draft. Retention/loss counters remain bounded. Saturation cannot block native control/cleanup or compact durable authority.','Unconditional privacy exclusion and explicit scope boundary.')
edit(13,'tradeoffs',str(rows[12]['tradeoffs']).replace('ELM-PER obligations','ELM-QA-021/023 and ELM-REV-020/021')+' Measure under the actual ELM-QA-021/023 and ELM-REV-020/021 budget contract.','Correct inherited budget reference.')
ss=rows[13]['scenarios'];ss[1]['then']=ss[1]['then'].replace('the original recovery deadline remains enforced',"each affected operation's original deadline is unchanged and is not renewed by recovery")
edit(14,'scenarios',ss,'Do not invent a universal recovery deadline.')
edit(15,'status','deferred-conditional-draft','No product selection or extra mandatory release gate for export.')
edit(16,'ears','WHILE a shell focus scope is open, the host SHALL preserve an eligible focused control through unrelated publications and dispatch admitted keyboard or assistive activation only to that native AT-exposed identity, rejecting retired or changed-scope targets and applying the frozen fallback when focus becomes ineligible.','Focus identity and activation agree even without publication changes.')
edit(16,'pattern','state-driven','State invariant with current eligibility.')
edit(16,'guardrails','Publication, lease and incarnation captured at press remain authoritative at release. Preserve the surviving focused identity while eligible under the frozen per-surface policy; disabled-but-focusable controls remain focused when030 allows it, otherwise apply the declared fallback. Selection is distinct from focus. Keyed DOM is an implementation choice.','Fix removal-only wording; retain disabled-navigation policy.')
ss=rows[15]['scenarios'];ss.append({'name':'focus-without-publication','given':'Close has keyboard/native AT focus while another row is selected','when':'Enter or Space is admitted without an intervening publication','then':'only Close is invoked, no window intent is dispatched and selection cannot override focused identity'})
edit(16,'scenarios',ss,'Keyboard activation follows exposed focus without requiring a publication race.')
ss=rows[16]['scenarios'];ss[0]['then']="both projections expose the same refusal state for the same control identity and focus remains on the user's control; announcement count follows ELM-ADOPT-012";ss.append({'name':'stable-name-state-change','given':'a single-window group whose visible identity label is unchanged becomes active or pending','when':'native AT re-reads the control','then':'the accessible name remains aligned with the same visible label while state/description changes under the frozen naming policy'})
edit(17,'scenarios',ss,'Semantics is distinct from announcement behavior.')
edit(17,'guardrails',rows[16]['guardrails']+' Verify cross-surface relationships in the native AT tree; DOM-local relationships do not automatically cross WebView documents.','Native relationship proof required.')
edit(20,'ears','WHEN a shell action is unavailable or unresolved, the shell SHALL expose the correlated reason and safe next step, retain eligible focus and controls outside its dependency domain, and never queue, defer or automatically replay input not accepted in that state or a rejected or Unknown action.','Unavailable inputs are locally not accepted, not necessarily terminally Refused.')
edit(20,'guardrails','Unrelated refresh means an unchanged declared family/target dependency domain and must preserve a valid picker/focus. Do not require concurrent native transactions. Repeated input during Pending follows INTERACTION.md feedback policy and ELM-UI-015; no second intent or announcement storm.','Concrete existing feedback policy and scoped independence.')
ss=rows[19]['scenarios'];ss +=[{'name':'unrelated-observation-refresh','given':'a picker is open for a family','when':"an unrelated observation refresh completes with that family's dependency revision unchanged",'then':'picker identity and focus persist and no new intent is emitted'},{'name':'same-control-during-pending','given':'a native operation is Pending for a control','when':'the same control is activated again','then':'no second intent is emitted; one truthful not-accepted result is exposed under the frozen feedback policy without repeated announcement or later replay'}]
edit(20,'scenarios',ss,'Qualify refresh churn and Pending-input race.')
ss=rows[21]['scenarios'];ss[1]['then']='the closed demand remains cancelled and its existing owner/cleanup stays recorded; another authorized demand may use only independently available eligible capacity, never the held reservation before matching release'
edit(22,'scenarios',ss,'Demand closure does not globally prohibit unrelated authorized work.')
edit(27,'ears','WHILE authorized preview demand persists, WHEN tracked source content advances during outstanding capture, the provider SHALL retain bounded latest-revision demand and service it under the frozen pacing policy after eligible capacity returns, admitting none after closure or revocation.','Bound recurring rate as well as queue size.')
edit(27,'guardrails',rows[26]['guardrails']+' Pacing/refresh is frozen in the existing budget matrix before qualification; continuous change cannot create unbounded back-to-back capture. Latest revision is limited to native-tracked coverage, currently root-surface commits only; no subsurface/family fidelity expansion.','Do not silently claim missing source coverage.')
ss=rows[26]['scenarios'];ss.append({'name':'continuous-change-and-final-revision','given':'authorized visible demand, continuously changing tracked content and eventually available eligible capacity','when':'the provider runs and then content change stops','then':'capture follows the frozen pacing policy, the final tracked revision is serviced when eligible, and presentation impact is measured under026 with no original deadline renewal'})
edit(27,'scenarios',ss,'Pacing and final-update liveness under explicit admission assumptions.')
